    11	**Hook point for projection writes.** The `persist(state, ...)` step of each adapter. It already receives every row of the transaction (data rows, journal rows, and retractions with their retraction columns applied) and builds one engine submit.
    12	
    13	- XTDB: `packages/xtdb/src/XtdbStorageAdapter.ts:188-331` (statement list `:193-267`, single `client.submit` `:290`, called from `:405-406`).
    14	- QLever: `packages/qlever/src/QleverStorageAdapter.ts:187-278` (VALUES list `:194-215`, single SPARQL UPDATE `:230`, called from `:343-344`).
    15	- The projection spec arrives through the runtime options bag that already feeds the adapter factory (`packages/xtdb/src/index.ts:14-22, 45-58`; QLever `index.ts:14-21, 46`).
    16	- Projection needs **zero edits** to `TriplesLive.ts`, `StorageAdapter.ts`, `Runtime.ts`, `KvTriplesLive.ts` or `packages/testkit`.
    17	
    18	**Journal finding.** An adapter can serve `transaction`, `transactionByCommand`, `transactions`, `transactionsForEntity` and the receipts without stored `:_tx/change` JSON, because every field of a `TransactionChange` is a column of the ledger row. Two things block a fully native journal and one thing makes a slimmer one safe.
    19	
    20	- Adapters never see `TransactionMeta` (actor, correlation, causation, config snapshot), so something must still store one small envelope per transaction.
    21	- `_Transaction` facts are public. Docs promise them to Datalog (`docs/operational-primitives.md:39-51`) and two of the 44 shared cases read them directly (`packages/testkit/src/index.ts:1728` and `:2612`). A fully native journal breaks those two cases.
    22	- Safe first step ("slim journal"): stop writing only the two O(changes) attributes (`:_tx/change`, `:_tx/changed-entity`), keep the O(1) envelope facts. All 44 cases keep passing, and stored rows drop by about half at large transactions.
