   136	
   137	- The extra read runs inside the replay loop, so it uses the same cut as the CAS. A concurrent commit changes `tx_meta.position`, the first ASSERT fails, and the whole attempt (read, plan, write) reruns.
   138	- Cost: one additional batched read per transaction that touches a projected entity type. `EntityStore.replace` already issues the same read before it writes (`packages/http/src/EntityStore.ts:201`).
   139	- With no spec the new lines are skipped, so the generated statement list is unchanged. R4's mock-client trace (`R4-test-outputs/xtdb-statement-trace.mts`) can pin that.
   140	- QLever: the same plan step sits at `:342-344`; the plan renders into the same `values` array (`:194-215`). The existing `DELETE ... INSERT ... OPTIONAL ?old` form replaces one object per `(subject, predicate)`, so multi-valued attributes need explicit deletes of removed objects. That is for the QLever lane to design. Note R4 section 4.3: failure atomicity inside a QLever UPDATE is unqualified, so a partial apply of ledger plus projection is possible in an engine-fault case. The `projection_position` fence in section 3.4 detects it.
   141	
   142	### 1.6 Rules the planner must follow (affect what the hook may do)
   143	
   144	1. **The ledger write must never fail because of projection data.** A value whose family does not match the declared type, a second value on a cardinality-one attribute, or an unknown attribute on a projected type sets `_shape_ok = false` on that entity's row (or records it in an overflow column) instead of raising. This keeps the ledger schema-less. The repository falls back to the ledger decode, which raises the same `DataShapeConflictError` `EntityCodec` raises today (`packages/http/src/EntityCodec.ts:186-234`).
   145	2. **Membership rule.** An entity belongs to type X when at least one live fact has `entity_type = X`. This is the same rule `entityPage` uses (`TriplesLive.ts:606`) and `encodeEntity` uses (`EntityCodec.ts:193-201`). Facts without an `entity_type` still contribute values to an entity that is a member by other facts.
   146	3. **Leaving a type.** When the last live type-X fact is retracted, the planner emits a delete for that entity's row in table X.
   147	4. **Valid-time window.** Facts have `valid_from` and `valid_to`. A row computed at the transaction instant `I` is correct only for `validAt` in `[I, B)`, where `B` is the earliest `valid_from > I` or `valid_to > I` among the entity's live facts. Store `_asof = I` and `_until = B` (null when none). See section 4.2 for how readers use them. This mirrors what `Triples.dependencyState` already computes as `nextTemporalBoundary` (`Triples.ts:150-155`).
   148	5. **Position.** Store `_position = state.position` per row and a per-scope `projection_position` that is updated on every commit, including commits that touch no projected entity.
   149	6. **State content id.** The planner can compute `hashCanonical(canonicalize(triplesToAttributeMap(facts)))` (exported from `internal.ts`, `snapshots/canonical.ts`) and store it as `_state_cid`. A verifier can then recompute from the ledger and compare, using the same id `EntitySnapshot.hash` uses today.
