   176	| Order of `changes[]` | op order inside the transaction | **No.** Only asserts are ordered (monotonic ULIDs, `utils/id.ts:52`, unless a deterministic id generator is used). Interleaving of retracts and asserts is lost. |
   177	| Which transactions are journaled | presence of `_Transaction` facts | Not from data rows. Unjournaled system writes (`ConsumerCheckpoint.ts:222, 266`, via `systemNamespace.ts:39-48`) still write ledger rows and consume positions. |
   178	| Entity to transaction index | `:_tx/changed-entity` | **Yes.** Positions at which any row of the entity was inserted (`recorded_position`) or retracted (`retracted_position`), intersected with journaled positions. |
   179	
   180	So the answer is yes for the O(changes) part and for the lookups, and no for the O(1) envelope. One stored envelope per transaction stays.
