   274	
   275	## 3. Schema at the adapter (question 3)
   276	
   277	### 3.1 How definitions exist at runtime
   278	
   279	| Form | Where | What it holds |
   280	|---|---|---|
   281	| `Attribute.Definition` | `config/Attribute.ts:26-37, 93-131` | key (`:ns/name`), `TypeExpr`, node `Effect`, encoder |
   282	| `Attribute.Use` | `Attribute.ts:39-52, 134-140` | `required`, `cardinality`, `unique` (widened to `boolean` / `"one" \| "many"`) |
   283	| `EntityType` object | `config/EntityType.ts:41-61` (type), `:69-154` (`make`) | `entityType`, `schema: TypeExpr.Struct` keyed by attribute key, `attributes` handles keyed by TypeScript alias, `constraints`, lazy `node` Effect |
   284	| Released node | `ConfigNode` kind `"entity-schema"`, key = entity type | `attrs.{entityType, type: Struct, attributes: {alias -> {attribute, required, cardinality, unique}}}` (`EntityType.ts:125-141`) plus `kind "attribute"` nodes with `attrs.{key, valueType}` |
   285	| Descriptor compiled from a release | `packages/http/src/ConfigApi.ts:143-380` | `EntityDescriptor {entityType, attributes: {key, alias, type, required, cardinality, unique, storage}}`. It already maps `TypeExpr` to the stored family (`ConfigApi.ts:66-102`: text/date to string, int64 to integer, instant to datetime, ref, List/Struct to json) and cross-checks the Struct against the usage metadata (`:282-294, 310-320`). |
   286	| Parsed schema only | `EntityValidation.parseDefinition` (`EntityValidation.ts:220-235`) | `{entityType, type: TypeExpr}` from `attrs` alone |
   287	
   288	Aliases are not identity (ARCHITECTURE.md ontology paragraph, cited in R3 section 2.1). The Struct (`fields[key] = {type, optional, fallback}`, `List` wrapper for cardinality many) already carries keys, types, requiredness and cardinality. Only `unique` lives in the constraint children. A projection spec needs none of the aliases.
   289	
   290	### 3.2 Options for giving the adapter a spec
   291	
   292	| Option | How | Problem or benefit |
   293	|---|---|---|
   294	| A. Layer option from `EntityType` objects | `makeXtdbRuntime({url, projection: ProjectionSpec.fromEntityTypes([...])})`, flowing into `makeXtdbStorageAdapter(client, scope, {projection})` at `xtdb/src/index.ts:46` | No cycle. Spec is pure data, known at process start, and its content id is computed without I/O. Can drift from the live release. |
   295	| B. Live `ConfigStore` release | adapter reads `resolveRef("live")` | **Circular.** `ConfigStore.layer` requires `Triples` (`ConfigStore.ts:495`), and `Triples` requires the adapter (`Runtime.ts:113-116`). The release commit is itself a transaction through the same adapter, so the very first write has no spec yet. A per-transaction release read costs a Datalog-free scan of config facts. A mutable registry swapped on `setRef` would work but adds ordering hazards. |
   296	| C. Both | A is authoritative for the adapter. At startup and on `setRef`, compute `ProjectionSpec.fromRelease(snapshot)` and compare content ids with A. | Detects drift without feeding the adapter from the store. One extra check. |
   297	
   298	**Recommendation: C, built on A.** Precisely: `ProjectionSpec.compile(definitions)` takes `{entityType, schema: Struct}[]`. `EntityType` objects supply `.entityType` and `.schema` directly. A release supplies the same pair via `parseDefinition`, or via the `ConfigApi.compile` descriptors once those live in core (section 5). Both paths hash the same canonical form, so equal content gives equal ids.
   299	
   300	Content id inputs (proposal): per entity type sorted by name, per attribute sorted by key: `{key, TypeExpr.canonical(type), required, cardinality}`, hashed with `ContentId.hash("triplex/projection-spec", canonicalJson)`. Reuse `TypeExpr.id/canonical` (`TypeExpr.ts:201-206`) and `CanonicalJson.encodeOrThrow` (`content/CanonicalJson.ts:138`). Add the domain next to the others at `content/ContentId.ts:30-56`. Aliases, `unique` and the attribute-node cids are excluded on purpose, so renaming an alias never changes the id. Whether `unique` should affect the spec is a decision: it has no physical column effect in the first version.
   301	
   302	### 3.3 Reserved types
   303	
   304	The spec compiler must reject or skip `_Transaction` and `triplex.*` entity types and `:triplex/`, `:_tx/` attributes. `ConfigApi.compile` already refuses them (`ConfigApi.ts:170, 203`). Config and validation writes go through `transactSystem` (`ConfigStore.ts:426, 439, 451`) and carry `triplex.config-*` types, which the planner ignores.
   305	
   306	### 3.4 Schema change, projection version, backfill
   307	
   308	Releases are immutable snapshots; `live` is a ref moved by compare-and-retract (`ConfigStore.setRef`, `ConfigStore.ts:446`). A new release with a changed entity type yields a different spec id. `InMemoryConfigStore.changesBetween(store, from, to)` (`InMemoryConfigStore.ts:473-525`) gives `ObjectAdded/Removed/Changed` by `(kind, key)`, and `TypeSubsumption.subsumes(from, to)` (`TypeSubsumption.ts:279`) returns `Identical | Widens | Narrows` per type.
   309	
   310	| Change | Spec effect | Backfill |
   311	|---|---|---|
   312	| Alias rename, constraint-only change | same id | none |
   313	| New optional attribute | new column | needed only if the ledger already holds facts under that key (facts are schema-less), found by a ledger scan on that attribute |
   314	| Attribute removed | column ignored or dropped | none (ledger keeps facts) |
   315	| `Identical` or `Widens` type change | column kept or widened | none or recompute that column |
   316	| `Narrows` or storage family change | new physical column or table | rebuild affected types |
   317	| New entity type | new table | scan `entity_type = X` |
   318	
   319	Fences and procedure (proposal):
   320	
   321	1. **Spec fence.** The projection meta row stores `spec_id` and `projection_position`. Every `persist` adds one ASSERT that `spec_id` equals the writer's spec id, so a writer with a stale spec fails closed (typed error) instead of corrupting the projection during a rolling deploy.
   322	2. **Rebuild.** At startup, if the stored `spec_id` differs, build shadow tables at position `P0`: scan the ledger by entity type, write rows. Catch up using the ledger itself, because entities changed since `P0` are `SELECT DISTINCT entity_id ... WHERE recorded_position > P0 OR retracted_position > P0`. No journal is needed. Switch `spec_id` in a single engine transaction guarded by `ASSERT tx_meta.position = P_head`. Retry catch-up on assertion failure.
   323	3. **Dual write** (alternative to catch-up): the option accepts `{active, building}` and writes both while rebuilding. Simpler to reason about, costs double write.
   324	4. Both need a typed admin entry point; both are adapter-package code, not core.
   325	
   326	---
   327	
   328	## 4. Read path (question 4)
   329	
   330	### 4.1 Which API reaches which adapter call
   331	
   332	| Public API | Core path | Adapter or executor call | Can a projection serve it unchanged? |
   333	|---|---|---|---|
   334	| `entity(id, basis)` | `TriplesLive.ts:571-576` | `getByEntity` | **No.** Returns `Triple[]` with per-fact id, `recordedAt`, `validFrom`, `validTo`, `createdBy`, `txId`, `retractedAt` (`rowToTriple` `:79-135`). A projection holds values only. |
   335	| `entities(ids, basis)` | `:578-583` | `getByEntities` | No, same reason. |
   336	| `entityPage(request)` | `:585-619` | `query({entityType}, basis)` for ids, then `getByEntities` | Bodies no. The **id discovery** step (`:606-610`) reads every fact of the type, then dedupes, sorts and slices. A projection could serve the id list at the current basis if rows were valid (section 4.2). Optional later optimization. Not exercised by the 44 cases (zero uses in `testkit/src/index.ts`). |
   337	| `match(pattern, basis)` | `:621-626` | `query` | No (`Triple[]`). |
   338	| `history(id)` | `:628-632` | `history` | No (needs retracted facts). |
   339	| Datalog `query/queryPage/queryAll/explain` | `:688-761` | `QueryExecutor.execute` (`storage/QueryExecutor.ts:115-166`) | No. Must stay on the ledger compilers. |
   340	| Journal reads | `:634-682` | `query({entityType:"_Transaction"})` | Section 2. |
   341	| `currentPosition`, `dependencyState` | `:780-786` | `currentCommitPosition`, `dependencyState` | Ledger only. |
   342	| Entity snapshots | `SnapshotService` (SQL tables) | `rawQuery` | Not available on XTDB or QLever (`SnapshotServiceLive.ts:75, 261`). |
   343	| Native queries | `makeXtdbNativeQueries(client, scope)` separate from `Runtime` (`native/NativeQueries.ts:35-192`) | read `tx_meta` cut, run caller SQL or XTQL over `facts()` (`native/Sources.ts:44-118`) | The projection can appear as a new native relation guarded by the row window rules. That is the native lane's work. |
   344	
   345	**Conclusion.** No existing `Triples` read can switch to a projection without changing what it returns. The projection serves only new surfaces: `Repository.get/find/count` returning typed documents, and native relations. That is why the 44 cases cannot see it.
   346	
   347	### 4.2 When a projection row answers a current-basis read
   348	
   349	The repository's "current basis" is `recordedAt` omitted (latest), `recordedPosition` = head, `validAt` = clock now (`Temporal.ts:44-61`; `EntityPage.ts:119-130`).
   350	
   351	```
   352	Entity read:  use the row iff
   353	   cut is the head:        projection_position == currentPosition
   354	   AND time in window:     row._asof <= validAt AND (row._until IS NULL OR validAt < row._until)
   355	   AND row._shape_ok
   356	 otherwise fall back to Triples.entity(id, basis) + the same decoder.
   357	
   358	Set read (find/count/page ids): use the table iff
   359	   cut is the head AND no row of the type has _until <= validAt
   360	 (one LIMIT 1 probe). Otherwise fall back to the ledger path.
   361	```
   362	
   363	Rows whose window has passed ("stale") are re-projected by a temporal refresh that recomputes entities with `_until <= now` from the ledger, in an engine transaction guarded by `ASSERT tx_meta.position = P`. This is a projection-only write, not a Triplex transaction. It is not needed for correctness (the fallback covers it) and is a follow-up for performance. Models with future-dated facts (start dates) will hit the fallback until it exists.
   364	
   365	Clock caution: tests with a deterministic clock (`Runtime.ts:68-82`) can read at a `now` earlier than `_asof`. The rule above falls back in that case.
   366	
   367	Ordering caution: `entityPage` orders ids with JavaScript's default `sort()` (`TriplesLive.ts:608`), which is UTF-16 code-unit order. A projection ordered by the engine may differ for ids with characters above the BMP. Add a parity test before the repository paginates from a projection.
   368	
