   371	## 5. Repository placement (question 5)
   372	
   373	### 5.1 Where
   374	
   375	A new core subpath, as R3 section 1.3 D4 recommends, for example `@triplex-build/triplex/entity`.
   376	
   377	- Add to `packages/core/package.json` `exports` (`exports` starts at `package.json:34`; `./operational` is the closest template).
   378	- `tsdown.config.ts` builds `src/**/*.ts` unbundled, so new files under `src/entity/` are picked up with no config change.
   379	- `vitest.workspace-aliases.ts` derives aliases from `exports`, so tests resolve the subpath to `src/` with no change.
   380	- `packages/http` already depends on core (`packages/http/package.json` dependencies). `packages/dashboard` depends on core, postgres and sqlite, not http (`packages/dashboard/package.json`), so a core subpath is the only shared home for both.
   381	
   382	### 5.2 What to reuse instead of rewriting
   383	
   384	| Existing code | Location | Reuse |
   385	|---|---|---|
   386	| Release to descriptor compile, including the stored-family mapping, duplicate and reserved checks, schema-versus-usage cross-check | `packages/http/src/ConfigApi.ts:143-380` | Move to `./entity` as `compileDescriptors(snapshot)`. This is also the best input for `ProjectionSpec`. |
   387	| Facts to typed document, with membership check, mixed-type rejection, decode through `TypeSchema.compile`, cardinality-one violation, missing-required | `packages/http/src/EntityCodec.ts:154-234` (`decodeStoredValue`, `encodeEntity`) | Move. It is the decode the repository's ledger path and the projection fallback must share, so both paths return the same documents and the same shape errors. |
   388	| Input to ops (normalization, closed schema, distinct sorted values) | `EntityCodec.ts:59-152` | Move for the Writer. |
   389	| Effect schemas per entity (`attributesSchema`, `outputSchema`) | `EntityCodec.ts:47-69` | Keep in http or move; core needs only decode. |
   390	| Create, replace, delete as `TransactOp[]` with `EntityState` preconditions and `enforce` from the pinned release | `packages/http/src/EntityStore.ts:100-247` | Template for the Writer (`create` = `assertOperations`, `replace` = retract live facts plus assert, preconditions from `triples.entity`). |
   391	| List through `entityPage` plus decode | `EntityStore.ts:127-152` | The repository's `find` fallback is exactly this. |
   392	| Value to stored-family mapping | `ConfigApi.ts:66-102`; `TypeSchema.compile/normalize` (`TypeSchema.ts:162-185`) | Reuse. |
   393	| Facts to attribute map and content id | `snapshots/canonical.ts` | Use for `_state_cid`. |
   394	| Whole-entity materialization for validation | `EntityValidation.materialize` (`:263-294`) | Different job (lenient, for hashing). Do not use for the repository. |
   395	
   396	Extraction detail: `EntityCodec` throws `DataShapeConflictError` and `RequestValidationError`, which are HTTP-API error classes with a `code` field (`packages/http/src/Errors.ts:1-68`). In core define neutral errors (`EntityShapeError {entityId, path, message}`, `EntityInputError {path, message}`) and have `packages/http` map them to its error classes. The two http tests (`packages/http/test/config-api.test.ts`, `integer-codec.test.ts`) guard behavior during the move.
   397	
   398	### 5.3 Type-level prerequisite
   399	
   400	R3 section 5.1: `Attribute.use` and `EntityType` handles widen `required` and `cardinality` (`Attribute.ts:46-52, 134-140`; `EntityType.ts:24-40`), and `Attribute.ref` forgets its target (`Attribute.ts:121-131`). The typed `Doc`, `Include` and `Input` types need them preserved. This is compile-time only, but it touches types used across 300-entity catalogs, so it must pass `pnpm --filter @triplex-build/triplex bench:config:typecheck` (`packages/core/package.json` scripts, `bench/config/typecheck-budget.mjs`).
   401	
   402	### 5.4 Reading the projection from the repository
   403	
   404	Engine-neutral first: repository over `Triples` plus the shared decoder. For projection reads, follow the existing precedent for engine-specific read factories that sit beside the runtime and take `(client, scope)`: `makeXtdbNativeQueries` (`xtdb/src/index.ts:90`) and `makeXtdbMaintainedQueries` (`index.ts:84`). A `makeXtdbProjectionReader(client, scope, spec)` plugs into the repository as an optional argument. This needs no change to `Runtime.define`. One consequence: the runtime's `Connection` is private to `makeXtdbRuntime` (`xtdb/src/index.ts:24`), so the reader opens its own client with the same URL and scope, as native queries do today.
