   408	## 6. Conformance impact (question 6)
   409	
   410	The 44 cases are `triplesConformanceCases` (`packages/testkit/src/index.ts:82-2863`). They run serially against one runtime and one scope (`makeTriplesConformanceSuite`, `:2865-2867`), through `runtimeConformance(runtime, {scope, capabilities})` (`:2869-2898`). Drivers: `packages/xtdb/test/conformance.test.ts:9-30` (240 s budget), `packages/qualification/test/runtime-conformance.test.ts:15-34`, KV oracle `packages/testkit/test/fixtures.test.ts:24-32`. All pass `Capabilities.none` and build the runtime with no projection or journal option.
   411	
   412	### 6.1 Projection
   413	
   414	- Every case uses the `Triples` API only (verified by reading the cases that touch entity types, reads and journal; no case reads engine tables).
   415	- No `Triples` read is served from the projection (section 4.1), so no result can change.
   416	- A runtime with **no spec** must produce byte-identical statements to today. Pin with R4's mock-client traces (`R4-test-outputs/xtdb-statement-trace.mts`, `qlever-triple-count.mts`).
   417	- A runtime **with** a spec that lists the conformance entity types (`Person`, `Robot`, `HistorySubject`, `ConfUser`, `ConfMembership`, `ConfGroup`, `TransactionPerson`, `TransactionRobot`, `Widget`, `ConfConstraintPerson`, `ConfConstraintEmployer`) must still pass all 44. What it can change is timing and conflicts, not results. Watch these cases:
   418	  - 30 "conditional transactions..." (two concurrent command claims, `:1859-1889`)
   419	  - 32 "graph constraints reject..." (position must not move on rejection, `:2036-2060`; one concurrent claimant, `:2144-2182`)
   420	  - 36 "consumer checkpoints..." (concurrent advance, `:2441-2464`)
   421	  - the whole-suite 240 s budget (`xtdb/test/conformance.test.ts:30`)
   422	  The conformance data also writes attributes such as `:age` and `:name` with no declared types on those entity types, which exercises the `_shape_ok` rule in section 1.6.
   423	
   424	### 6.2 Journal, by case (numbers are the order in `triplesConformanceCases`)
   425	
   426	| # | Case | Line | Observes | T1 | T2 |
