I accept two section C pushbacks: an early repository skeleton is fine if it follows independently frozen contracts, and rare interior XTDB cuts can use an exact ledger fallback. The remaining blockers are the full-basis selector, log commit/recovery semantics, fencing every QLever mutation, and defining how partial or conflicted entities affect whole queries.
